  "period_note": "Year-end (31 December 2015) position, SOLO basis, primarily from the bank's own audited Balance Sheet, Profit and Loss Account and the 'Highlights on the overall activities of the bank' annexure in that year's own annual report. EPS restatement found: this year's own report states EPS Tk.0.88 (PAT 358,006,980 / 408,960,000 shares, paid-up capital unchanged at Tk.4,089,600,000). The FY2016 annual report's comparative column instead shows FY2015 EPS as Tk.0.83 -- this is the arithmetically-correct BAS 33 retrospective bonus-share adjustment (358,006,980 / 433,497,600 post-6%-bonus shares = 0.83), because Tk.245,376,000 of paid-up capital (a 6% stock dividend declared out of FY2015 profit) was issued during 2016. This dataset keeps the FY2015 contemporaneous (pre-bonus) EPS of 0.88, consistent with the standing rule to prefer contemporaneous figures; see sources.json for the general note on this bank's recurring EPS/NAV bonus-restatement pattern (it recurs in most subsequent years and is not treated as a data error). Tier-I (CET1, 4,556.68m) / Tier-II (net of 20%-for-2015 revaluation-reserve deduction, 228.49m) from the Basel III Pillar III 'Quantitative Disclosures' table.",
